; jmpr_chain36.simi — M2.60: the fold fixpoint's RELAXATION 2-CYCLE, the
; last documented-but-untested convergence mechanism. The M2.18 comment
; names it: "a fold ENABLED BY the relaxation can target the relaxed head
; itself (a backward fold re-entering the head makes it a loop head the
; relaxation must not apply to) — that shape 2-cycles the fixpoint
; (relax -> fold -> reset -> un-fold)". The head V (pc 5) is relax-
; eligible: the UNIQUE forward edge into it is S's BR (pc 3), V-1 = pc 4
; is a RET (terminal), no CALL targets it, it is not an entry. JMPR J
; (pc 8) dispatches on r2 = V (pc 5) — a BACKWARD fold re-entering V —
; and r2's constant (LOADI at pc 2) is established BEFORE V, so the
; reset at the pre-marked head V kills it UNLESS the relaxation restores
; it from the S snapshot. That is precisely "a fold enabled by the
; relaxation":
;
;   pass 1:  snapshot at S -> relax restores r2 at V -> J folds to V
;   pass 2:  V is now a fold target -> relaxation excluded -> reset
;            kills r2 -> J un-folds
;   pass 3:  V no longer a fold target -> relax again -> J folds
;   ...      2-cycle forever (relax -> fold -> reset -> un-fold) ...
;   pass 513: the 512-pass safety net fires: relax disabled, fold set
;            cleared, restart. The un-relaxed fixpoint is monotone-
;            decreasing in the fold set and terminates: pass 1 resets
;            r2 at V (no relaxation), J never folds; pass 2 confirms.
;
; The final converged state — J un-folded — is the SAME the un-relaxed
; analysis would reach, so the net's restart is sound (the pin proves
; termination, not a different emission: the gate row is identical to a
; no-relaxation build; the four-way parity proves the runtime result).
; J is the single dynamic JMPR -> the M2.25 walk runs: its snapshot at J
; is {5} (the S-branch delivers {5} at the head V; the loop back-edge is
; NOT an edge for the walk — an unfolded JMPR is a terminal — so the
; walk converges in 2 iterations and the M2.58 guard stays silent). The
; 1-candidate chain dispatches r2 = 5 back to V, the loop runs three
; times (r1 3->2->1->0), the BC exits at r1 == 0, r0 = 5 + 5 = 10.
; The teeth: Control A (head not relax-eligible) takes ~3 passes with
; no net; Control B (net disabled, timeout-bounded) HANGS on the
; 2-cycle (exit 124) — the net is the termination mechanism. Both are
; instrumentation-level, not emission-level: the pin guards termination.
; Expected result: 10 (r0 = r2+r2 = 5+5; the loop body runs twice)
.entry main
main:
    ENTER #8
    LOADI r1, #3, i64        ; loop counter (3 iterations)
    LOADI r2, #5, i64        ; J's index = V's pc — the constant the
                             ; relaxation must restore at V (source BEFORE V)
S:  BR V                     ; pc 3 — the unique forward edge into V
    RET                      ; pc 4 — dead (BR never falls through); V-1 is a
                             ; terminal, making V relax-eligible
V:  SUB r1, r1, #1, i64      ; pc 5 — the loop head, relax-eligible
    BC r1, EXIT, INV         ; pc 6 — exit when r1 == 0
    ADD r0, r0, r2, i64      ; pc 7 — body: r0 += 5 (r1 = 2, then 1)
    JMPR r2                  ; pc 8 — J: backward fold to V iff the
                             ; relaxation restored r2 (the 2-cycle source)
EXIT:
    ADD r0, r0, #0, i64      ; pc 9 — r0 = 10
    RET
